<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  BoxedVN ships exactly two entitlements, and each one is load-bearing.

	  get-task-allow
	      Lets a debugger attach to the app.  That is the mechanism StikDebug
	      and equivalent JIT enablers use; a successful attach gets the kernel
	      to flag the process CS_DEBUGGED, which relaxes code-signing
	      enforcement for plain mmap()/mprotect() PROT_EXEC transitions on
	      that process (NOT the same thing as macOS's MAP_JIT - MAP_JIT
	      itself stays gated behind Apple's "dynamic-codesigning" entitlement,
	      which is approved only for browser engines and is never obtainable
	      by a sideloaded app, debugger attached or not - see
	      include/boxedwine.h's MAP_BOXEDWINE and
	      ios/runtime/src/BVNJIT.mm).  Without get-task-allow no debugger can
	      attach at all, and Boxedwine's ARM64 JIT cannot run.  Sideloading
	      tools normally set this themselves; it is declared here so an
	      unsigned IPA carries the intent.

	  com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit
	      Boxedwine reserves a large contiguous region for the emulated guest
	      address space.  Without the raised limit the app is jetsammed on
	      devices with less RAM.  This entitlement is honoured only when the
	      signing identity is allowed to use it; free Apple IDs are not, and
	      signing tools strip it.  BoxedVN works without it on 6 GB+ devices,
	      so it is safe to remove.

	  Entitlements deliberately NOT present:
	      com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit and friends are macOS Hardened
	      Runtime keys and mean nothing on iOS.
	      com.apple.private.* keys require Apple-internal signing.
	      No hypervisor, USB or jailbreak entitlements: BoxedVN emulates in
	      userspace and needs none of them.

	  See docs/BUILD_IOS.md for what a signing tool may rewrite or drop.
	-->
	<key>get-task-allow</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
